<resources>
    <string name="dom_title">Egyptian Dominoes</string>
    <string name="dom_tagline">Seven tiles. Two ends. One real table.</string>
    <string name="dom_subtitle">2–4 players · Same Wi-Fi</string>
    <string name="dom_open">Take a seat</string>
    <string name="dom_rules">Double-six, seven tiles each. The highest dealt double opens; the hand winner leads next. Match either open end. In Draw, take tiles from the ordered stock only when nothing fits, stopping as soon as you can play. In Block, there is no drawing. Pass only when you cannot play or draw. Going out scores opponents’ pips. A blocked hand scores opponents’ pips minus the winner’s own; a lowest tie scores nobody. Doubles are not spinners. Reach the target; after 64 hands the highest score wins.</string>
